---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CyberArchive from '../components/CyberArchive.astro';
import CyberTicker from '../components/CyberTicker.astro';
---
<Base title="U.S. Cybersecurity Updates" description="National cyber incident reporting and a searchable archive of public breach notices and federal advisories.">
  <main class="container cyber-updates-page">
    <header class="cyber-updates-intro">
      <p class="overline">Public reporting</p>
      <h1>U.S. Cybersecurity Updates</h1>
      <p>Nationally reported incidents, breach notices, and federal advisories. This is public reporting, not live attack telemetry or part of DAL-X execution enforcement.</p>
      <p>Published snapshot: November 21, 2026. Updates are not yet automatic.</p>
    </header>
    <CyberTicker />
    <section class="national" aria-labelledby="national-title"><p class="overline">Reviewed coverage</p><h2 id="national-title">National incidents</h2><p>Nationally reported U.S. incidents and consequential disclosures, reviewed separately from the automated feeds. Dates mark the linked coverage or disclosure, not when the intrusion began.</p><ul><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-21">2026-11-21</time><span>Company statement to press</span></p><h3>Microsoft Entra Connect Health: tenant metadata exposed</h3><p>Microsoft confirmed to BleepingComputer that it fixed the security issue and notified affected customers. The number of organizations affected was not disclosed.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/microsoft-entra-connect-health-flaw-exploited-to-steal-tenant-data/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BleepingComputer</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-20">2026-11-20</time><span>Media report; not independently confirmed</span></p><h3>USDA: intrusion into a farm-payment system reported</h3><p>NBC News reported that intruders accessed a system used for farmer payments, citing sources familiar with the incident. The scope of any data exposure remains unverified here.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/national-security/agriculture-department-breached-hackers-sources-say-rcna610497" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NBC News</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-19">2026-11-19</time><span>Company statements to press</span></p><h3>Chase, Visa and Mastercard: customer data exposed at vendors</h3><p>The companies described third-party incidents involving limited customer information. Visa said its systems and card numbers were not affected.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://apnews.com/article/chase-data-leak-cyberattack-8470d475450721b66858bdace47091c0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Associated Press</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://abcnews.com/US/jpmorgan-chase-reports-cyberattack-party-service-providers/story?id=138287705" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ABC News</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-16">2026-11-16</time><span>State breach notice</span></p><h3>Uber: driver license data exposed through a service provider</h3><p>Uber’s notice describes unauthorized access through a service provider. TechCrunch reported that Uber was notifying close to 150,000 drivers.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://oag.ca.gov/ecrime/databreach/reports/sb24-632751" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">California DOJ</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/16/uber-confirms-hackers-stole-thousands-of-drivers-license-information-in-data-breach/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TechCrunch</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-09">2026-11-09</time><span>University disclosure</span></p><h3>Vanderbilt University: cyberattack disrupted campus IT</h3><p>Vanderbilt advised its community to shut down devices and disconnect from campus Wi-Fi while it contained the incident. The university was still investigating what data was accessed.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://news.vanderbilt.edu/2026/11/09/nov-9-active-cybersecurity-incident-updates/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vanderbilt University</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://www.washingtonpost.com/education/2026/11/09/vanderbilt-university-shuts-down-devices-after-cyber-attack/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Washington Post</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-04">2026-11-04</time><span>State breach notice</span></p><h3>DreamHost: customer files and email exposed</h3><p>DreamHost reported a breach that affected customer accounts, and TechCrunch reported access to files and email. The company did not publish a precise affected customer count in the reporting reviewed.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://oag.ca.gov/ecrime/databreach/reports/sb24-632268" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">California DOJ</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/04/hackers-stole-dreamhost-customer-files-and-inboxes-during-months-long-attack/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TechCrunch</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-22">2026-10-22</time><span>SEC filing, Item 8.01</span></p><h3>Quest Diagnostics: unauthorized access to lab services system</h3><p>Quest believes some patient records were accessed. The company filed under Other Events, not the dedicated material cybersecurity incident item.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1022079/000094787126000941/ss6979200_8k.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SEC EDGAR</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://apnews.com/article/quest-cyber-breach-82dbe1fa6ba06cf6514bc16f73e64fe1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Associated Press</a></p></li></ul></section>
    <CyberArchive />
  </main>
</Base>
<style is:global>
.cyber-updates-page{padding-block:clamp(2rem,6vw,5rem); min-width:0}
.cyber-updates-intro{margin-bottom:1.5rem}
.cyber-updates-intro h1{font-size:clamp(2rem,7vw,4.6rem);line-height:1.05;margin:.5rem 0 1rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}
.cyber-updates-intro p{color:#cdc2b9;max-width:70ch;line-height:1.55;margin:.45rem 0}
.cyber-updates-page .overline{font:.75rem ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#f1a373}
.national{margin-block:clamp(2rem,5vw,4.5rem);min-width:0}.national h2{margin:.2rem 0 .75rem;font-size:clamp(1.8rem,5vw,3rem);letter-spacing:-.04em;line-height:1.1}.national p{max-width:76ch;line-height:1.55;color:#cdc2b9}.national .overline{color:#f1a373}.national ul{list-style:none;margin:1.1rem 0 0;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,300px),1fr));gap:.85rem}.national li{background:#1c1917;border:1px solid #493a32;border-radius:.45rem;padding:1rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.national h3{margin:.35rem 0 .4rem;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.35}.national li p{margin:.35rem 0;font-size:.85rem}.national li .national-meta{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.15rem .65rem;font:.7rem ui-monospace,monospace;color:#f1a373}.national-links a{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-height:44px;color:#f4f0ec;text-underline-offset:.18em}.national-links a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #f1a373;outline-offset:2px}
</style>
